"eli5": "Picture a car wash. $V_{\\max}$ is the top speed when every bay is full. $K_m$ is how many cars must be waiting in line before the wash runs at half speed. A low $K_m$ wash gets busy even with a short line. But $K_m$ is not pure \"stickiness\": it mixes how well cars pull in ($k_1$, $k_{-1}$) with how fast they get washed ($k_{\\text{cat}}$). That's why we call it **apparent affinity**.",
