"eli5": "The MM graph is the real-life picture: add more substrate, the enzyme speeds up, then maxes out. The LB graph is a math trick: flip both numbers upside down and the curve straightens into a line, so the intercepts are easy to read. The catch: everything on LB is \"one over\" something, so you have to flip back.",
